<!-- 01 — APPROACH -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — Approach</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Graphic design rarely accounts for more than <span class="stat">ten per cent</span> of the actual effort in a mandate. The far larger part consists of getting inside the logic of manufacturers, distributors and end consumers — and understanding how a product or a technology is actually perceived across different touchpoints.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The core of the work lies in a single ability: translating technical product advantages — the "reason why" — into a benefit that can mean something different to each target group along the sales channel.</p>
  <a href="/en/approach/" class="btn-arrow reveal reveal-delay-2">The full approach →</a>
</section>

<!-- 02 — EXAMPLE -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — Example</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">What this looks like in practice</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The venting of a high-voltage battery in an electric vehicle is an inconspicuous component. Designed with a medium flow rate, the battery "breathes" in normal operation — and contaminates itself continuously in the process. Designed with a pressure relief valve that opens only in a thermal incident, it stays closed and clean in normal operation.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A technical detail only becomes a benefit promise once someone understands what it actually means for the end user: a significantly longer battery life in everyday use.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2">The same technical fact can be phrased as a warranty-cost argument for the manufacturer, as a durability promise for the end user, and as a sales argument against price-driven alternatives for a distributor. This act of translation — from the technical "reason why" to the benefit that matters to each target group — is at the centre of every mandate.</p>
</section>

<!-- 03 — LATITUDE -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">03 — Latitude</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Using the full latitude the regulations allow</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2">The same translation applies where a task is tightly defined by law. Lünstroth uses the available latitude to the full — for maximum effect, not just for compliance. For <a href="/en/case-studies/meisterhaft-zdb/" style="color:var(--accent);">Meisterhaft</a>, that meant turning a term that was purely descriptive, and therefore not protectable as a trademark, into a registrable mark — as close as possible to the meaningful message without losing the necessary distinctiveness.</p>
</section>

